    "available_at": "2026-11-24T23:22:55.240585+00:00",
    "body": "Great on any Friday: Google Pixel Buds Pro 2 (2025) - Bluetooth Earbuds with Active Noise Cancellation\nPorsche's ICE-Powered Macan Is Returning With a New Generation, Is This What It Will Look Like?\n10 photos\nPhoto: Instagram | avarvarii\nThe original Porsche Macan lived for 12 years, with production spanning from 2014 to 2026, and that’s a very impressive achievement by today’s standards.\nThe company pulled the plug on it earlier this year, which is when the final copy rolled off the line at the Leipzig factory in Germany. It utilized the MLB platform, just like the old Audi Q5, the B8 A4, and its sportier-looking sibling, the A5, from the same era, and was offered with gasoline and diesel power throughout the years, with manual and automatic transmissions.\nIn case you forgot, there is an entirely new Porsche Macan out, and it is a battery-electric model. Production started two and a half years ago, in the first half of 2024, and it put together at the same facility as its ICE predecessor. The Macan EV utilizes the PPE (Premium Platform Electric) architecture, just like its larger sibling, the Cayenne Electric, as well as Audi’s A6 e-tron, and Q6 e-tron, and the Bentley Torcal.\nGiven that the Macan has officially transitioned to the battery-electric era, one might be tempted to think that there won’t be a combustion-powered alternative anymore. But they would be wrong, you see, because the Zuffenhausen company is indeed preparing such a thing as we speak. We have seen in on a few occasions, in the open, including last month (October 2026), and it is that prototype (it was actually a test mule) that has been used to create a set of realistic renderings.\nPhoto: Instagram | avarvarii The pixel artist behind the digital illustrations shared in the gallery above is none other than @avarvarii. As for the CGI-infused model, it looks pretty much like an evolution of its predecessor, which isn’t exactly a surprise given that this is after all Porsche, and it’s not famously known for significantly altering the looks of its new models compared to the older ones. And that’s definitely a compliment these days.\nDon’t let the design trick you into thinking that it is another updated version of the first generation, because it isn’t. In fact, it will utilize the PPC (Premium Platform Combustion). The construction is the foundation stone of its lesser cousin, the new-gen Audi Q5, as well as the latest A5, A6, and Q7, and the first-ever Q9.\nPower-wise, it should share some assemblies with the latest Audi Q5, and this probably means a straight-four and a V6 gasoline burner, and perhaps a TDI four-banger for the European market. In the States, you can get the Q5 with 268 hp from $53,300 (MSRP), and the SQ5 with 362 hp from $65,900. Chances are the new ICE-powered Macan will be punchier.\nReports indicate the new ICE -powered Porsche Macan will probably arrive in late 2028, and that’s two years from now. If that’s the case, then it should arrive in USA for the 2029 model year. View this post on Instagram A post shared by Avarvarii Automotive Artworks (@avarvarii)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nPorsche Macan Porsche Macan 2029 Porsche Macan rendering renderings crossover\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT This Tucker, Built After the Factory Closed, Sat Hidden for 13 Years, Great-Grandsons Bring It Home",
